Per> - Let intrinsic protections have a (long) time-out.

marcs> No way, after working hard to get intrinsic teleport control
marcs> intrinsicly it would suck to loose it.

I meant intrinsic _armor_ protection timeout only.
 
Per> - Remove wands of wishing from the game.  Replace the wand with a
Per> magic lamp in the castle level. 

marcs> No, if you get past the castle, you deserve the wand.

5 - 7 wishes?  Wouldn't just one or two wishes be a great reward?

marcs> That is total s**t,this would hinder non lawful characters,
marcs> Excalibur is easy to get, but chaotics and nuetrals would be in
marcs> trouble. 

Sorry, I forgot about Excalibur from fountains.  It should probably be
(is it already) restricted to Knights.  To balance it, knights should
have some other disadvantages (intrinsic slowness? :-)
 
marcs> It would be hard to get to hell without a named weapon.

Then scale down the monsters.  Something should be done to make
ordinary weapons useful again.

Per> - Make intelligent monsters immune to conflict.

marcs> define intelligent. To many monsters could fit in that
marcs> cattegorie, making the ring almost useless.
 
It wouldn't be the ring of win game as it is now, but it would still
be a great help when fighting a mixed group of monsters.  The stupid
monsters would help you attack the intelligent monsters.

Per> - Make regeneration faster for low level characters, and slower for
Per> high-level characters compared to now.  

marcs> This would really suck at lower levels, high-levels characters
marcs> take more damage because they fight stronger monsters.

But they also have better armor and higher CON, so they would still be
better of.  I also think their regeneration should be faster than low
level characters, just not as much as now.

Per> - A chrysknife should be significantly better than all other non-named
Per> weapons.

marcs> Why? 

Because it has its own miniquest associated, and because a better
weapon would make named weapons unnecessary until Hell.

marcs> I think that you shouldn't sacrifice the fun of the game for
marcs> the sake of game ballance, and I think that most of these
marcs> suggestions would really make the game ballance worse, high
marcs> level characters would have a lower survival rate than low
marcs> ones. Once you get a character to high level, you get pissed if
marcs> you loose him or her.

Well, after you have got past the castle level, you are very unlikely
to die in an honest fight.  I think most high-level level characters
now die from stupid mistakes such as choking on their food, or picking
up a heavy corpse at the wrong moment.  And you have to play like that
for many hours more before finishing the game.  I would like the part
of the game after the castle level to be as fun as the part before the
castle.



